## Workflow Overrides (Repo Policy)
<!-- These directives refine/override general behaviors for this repository. -->

- Do NOT commit or push any edits until the user explicitly says "commit" after local testing and approval.
- Always work on the current feature branch; never push directly to `main`.
- Provide clear local test steps with each change and wait for user feedback before committing.
- Prefer small, incremental edits; avoid regenerating large files unnecessarily.

> Note: The first bullet overrides the generic rule "You must always commit your changes whenever you update code" for this repository. Commits happen only upon explicit user approval.